# Additional external paths hooks may access outside the harness root.
# Entries here are added to the built-in default allowlist — /tmp and
# every supported agent's own config dir (see load_allowed_ext_dirs in
# scripts/lib/rm-guard.sh) — so list only your own extras. Comma or colon
# separated; supports a leading `~` for $HOME. There is no blanket
# "allow everything outside the harness root" switch.
#
# Hooks read .env from the checkout root AND from the lab root (the
# directory holding repos/ + worktree/); both lists are combined. Put a
# single .env at the lab root to cover every checkout on the machine.
# Changes apply on the next tool call — .env is read per hook invocation.
# Example: ALLOWED_EXT_DIRS=~/scratch,~/work
ALLOWED_EXT_DIRS=
